<%# The rose bower's arrival curtain: two silk drapes that draw apart, where the gilded hall has
    banks of cloud.

    No photograph at all, unlike the gilded hall's. Cloud needed a picture because a gradient
    cannot fake the texture; silk is exactly the thing a repeating gradient DOES describe well -
    parallel folds catching light - so this curtain has nothing to download and is opaque from the
    stylesheet alone, which is the property the whole overlay depends on.

    The banks keep the shared .throne-intro__bank class: parting sideways, the skip-on-first-input
    behaviour and the bfcache replay in public/js/throne-intro.js all belong to the curtain as a
    concept, not to what it is made of. Only the material and the inner edge are this skin's.

    There is no seam element here. The cloud banks feather their inner edges into each other and
    need something opaque filling the overlap; a drape has a real hem, and the two simply meet. %>
<div class="throne-intro__bank throne-intro__bank--left rose-drape">
  <%# The hem: scallops with a hanging pearl in each, a fixed-size strip that is cropped rather
      than stretched down a tall viewport - a stretched scallop is not a scallop. %>
  <svg class="rose-drape__hem" viewBox="0 0 30 1200" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin slice" role="presentation">
    <% for (let i = 0; i < 30; i++) { const y = i * 40; %>
      <path d="M0 <%= y %> L14 <%= y %> A 15 20 0 0 1 14 <%= y + 40 %> L0 <%= y + 40 %> Z"
            fill="var(--throne-accent)" opacity="0.55" />
      <path d="M14 <%= y %> A 15 20 0 0 1 14 <%= y + 40 %>" fill="none"
            stroke="var(--throne-gold-bright)" stroke-width="2" opacity="0.75" />
      <circle cx="26" cy="<%= y + 20 %>" r="3" fill="var(--throne-gold-bright)" opacity="0.8" />
    <% } %>
  </svg>
</div>
<div class="throne-intro__bank throne-intro__bank--right rose-drape">
  <svg class="rose-drape__hem" viewBox="0 0 30 1200" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin slice" role="presentation">
    <% for (let i = 0; i < 30; i++) { const y = i * 40; %>
      <path d="M0 <%= y %> L14 <%= y %> A 15 20 0 0 1 14 <%= y + 40 %> L0 <%= y + 40 %> Z"
            fill="var(--throne-accent)" opacity="0.55" />
      <path d="M14 <%= y %> A 15 20 0 0 1 14 <%= y + 40 %>" fill="none"
            stroke="var(--throne-gold-bright)" stroke-width="2" opacity="0.75" />
      <circle cx="26" cy="<%= y + 20 %>" r="3" fill="var(--throne-gold-bright)" opacity="0.8" />
    <% } %>
  </svg>
</div>
